      "blob_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/adf84d55fcc4526fb1f279a3e0f90cb1f9ff6485/docs%2Fusage%2Fsecurity.md",
      "changes": 6,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/contents/docs%2Fusage%2Fsecurity.md?ref=adf84d55fcc4526fb1f279a3e0f90cb1f9ff6485",
      "deletions": 2,
      "filename": "docs/usage/security.md",
      "patch": "@@ -355,7 +355,7 @@ This is particularly concerning because the code being executed is generated by\n \n #### Controlling Built-in Tool Availability\n \n-Built-in demo tools are controlled by two settings:\n+The following settings control tool registration and MCP label mapping:\n \n 1. **`--tool-server demo`**: Enables the built-in demo tools (browser and Python code interpreter).\n \n@@ -366,7 +366,9 @@ Built-in demo tools are controlled by two settings:\n \n    If this variable is not set or is empty, no built-in tools requested via MCP tool type will be enabled.\n \n-To disable the Python code interpreter specifically, omit `code_interpreter` from `VLLM_GPT_OSS_SYSTEM_TOOL_MCP_LABELS`.\n+This allowlist applies only to tools requested via the `mcp` tool type. Native Responses API tool types, such as `code_interpreter` and `web_search_preview`, can select the corresponding registered tools independently of this variable. Omitting a label from the allowlist does not disable that tool for native requests.\n+\n+To prohibit Python tool execution, configure an external tool server that does not provide the `python` tool namespace instead of using `--tool-server demo`. For example, a browser-only tool server can provide browsing without Python execution. Omit `--tool-server` entirely if no server-side tool execution is needed.\n \n **Consider a custom implementation**: The GPT-OSS Python tool is a reference implementation. For production deployments, consider implementing a custom code execution sandbox with stricter isolation guarantees. See the [GPT-OSS documentation](https://github.com/openai/gpt-oss?tab=readme-ov-file#python) for guidance.\n ",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/raw/adf84d55fcc4526fb1f279a3e0f90cb1f9ff6485/docs%2Fusage%2Fsecurity.md",
